    "latestPrereqDate": "2027-06-18",
    "oldestPrereqDate": "Recent evidence of success in a rigorous academic program preferred.",
    "selectionFactors": "UConn accepts highly qualified CT residents, with special effort to include those who are disadvantaged. Highly qualified out-of-state residents are considered to achieve a class with varied experiences. UConn considers applicants\u2019 interests, achievements, abilities, motivation, and character. GPA and MCAT scores, academic achievement beyond regular coursework, intellectual growth and development, nonacademic activities, and recommendations are considered. UConn is strongly opposed to prejudice and discrimination and has a strong tradition of seeking diverse students with varied experiences. UConn prohibits discrimination in accordance with provisions of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX Education Amendments of 1972, the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Americans with Disabilities Act, and other federal and state laws and executive orders pertaining to equal rights pursuant to the University\u2019s Policy Against Discrimination, Harassment and Related Interpersonal Violence.",
